WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:17.770
My name is Joe Ng, and I'm the executive chef
of RedFarm and Decoy restaurants.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:21.620
My background in cooking comes from Hong Kong.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.290
I never went to culinary school.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.970
I grew up in the kitchen.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.140
I started to cook at 11 or 12-years-old.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.010
I was cooking street food in the beginning.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:34.980
Then I started working in restaurants after
a couple of years.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.760
Most Americans know about peking duck.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.440
We thought, "Why don't we try to do peking
duck in a different, less traditional way?"

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.440
We tried testing and creating more sauces
and made different kinds of vegetables.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.030
I make our own pancakes, and we butcher the
duck in a different way.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:58.790
Me and my partner try to put creativity into
our food, the plating, and the ingredients

00:00:58.790 --> 00:00:59.870
as well.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:04.970
When we prepare the duck at the beginning,
we wash the duck and try to get the skin as

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:09.160
clean as possible, otherwise it will turn
very dark or burn.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:13.830
We use ducks that are about six-and-a-half
to seven pounds.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.310
That size is really good for barbecue.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.440
The muscle and the meat is very balanced.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.110
We put all of the five-spice flavors in there,
as well as salt, ginger, and scallion.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:27.430
And then we use a special nail to close the
bottom.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:32.910
It's very important that the ducks come with
the head on, because we are pumping air in

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:36.670
their necks to try to separate the skin from
the meat

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:40.759
Then we put it in boiling water to get the
muscle tight.

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:47.729
We put sugar and vinegar on top of the duck,
which helps the skin not crack.

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:51.369
That's why they come out golden brown, because
of the sugar and the vinegar.

00:01:51.369 --> 00:01:58.259
We hang them for about 24 hours to make sure
the skin gets dry.

00:01:58.259 --> 00:02:01.580
The dryer they get, the more crispy the skin
gets as a result.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.149
We turn the oven to 450 degrees.

00:02:04.149 --> 00:02:08.899
We cook that for 15 minutes, and then turn
down the temperature to around 350.

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:11.680
It cooks for another thirty minutes.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:17.810
The last 10 minutes are very important, because
the fat drips down from the top to the bottom.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:20.420
We have a pan underneath that catches all
the duck fat.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:26.500
In general, people probably have about two
to three wraps per person for each duck.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.540
Here we have three to four sauces, but the
traditional way is only hoisin.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:31.540
That's it.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.739
What about using sesame peanut sauce or adding
cranberry sauce?

00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:38.770
I would like them to try different flavors,
so they don't feel bored.

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:43.909
There's a different kind of taste in each
wrap.

00:02:43.909 --> 00:02:50.390
Twenty to 30 years ago, people only knew about
American-Chinese food, which is served at

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:51.390
the take-out restaurants.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:55.920
The really traditional food that we ate at
home is not what you're going to buy from

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.150
the take-out restaurants.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:01.829
If all these Chinese people are eating traditional
Chinese food at home, why don't they serve

00:03:01.829 --> 00:03:03.200
that in the restaurants?

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:10.140
That's why we tried to create a different
menu with a new take on Chinese food.

